{"data": [{"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-10-30T15:16:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116187558946447732"], "id": "2116187558946447732", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 5137, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116182735459135910", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "For those interested in financial flows rather than current account measurement -- about $700 b of the $900b net financial outflow associated with China's external surplus looks to be in fx ... not in CNY https://t.co/3CEnNV802G https://t.co/GLG57hWv0m", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2116187558946447732"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-30T15:05:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116184826738856399"], "id": "2116184826738856399", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 37, "impression_count": 12537, "like_count": 92, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 21}, "text": "Adam Josephson at Sakonnet Research says the \"resilient consumer\" is a myth, and that more and more consumer staples companies are seeing revenue growth that's lower than inflation https://t.co/TTxtrMPNk9", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2116184826738856399"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-10-30T14:57:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116182562569892163", "2116182735459135910"], "id": "2116182735459135910", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 12, "impression_count": 9903, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "China's q3 current account surplus should come in around $270 billion (the BoP goods and services balance is out and it is $75b higher than q3 last year).   \n\nThat pushes the surplus over the last 4qs to around $900b/ over 4 pp of GDP \n\n1/ https://t.co/4B5Ewy6WvR", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2116182735459135910"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "