ours before that huge OpenAI drop of 200 open problems. And this one was recorded a few hours before the Binance hack. https://t.co/7Gk1iIXOGi", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2116163871534965140"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-30T13:41:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116163490742431765"], "id": "2116163490742431765", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12553, "like_count": 29, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116163122344177773", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "A little surprised binancecoin:native isn't down more, but the market is always right, so https://t.co/28SyooSgyZ", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2116163490742431765"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-30T13:37:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116162564530823475"], "id": "2116162564530823475", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 13, "impression_count": 21017, "like_count": 36, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 3}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116161844666581423", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "It's fascinating to hear how skilled hackers think.  And @XorNinja and @brucedang do a great job explaining the philosophy and practice of cybersecurity, both pre- and post-AI and how for now we're still in the \"centaur\" era of hacking, where man + computer is still the best. https://t.co/u334g9JQml", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2116162564530823475"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-30T13:33:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116161547651399989"], "id": "2116161547651399989", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1172, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116151581087572150", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "BTW, while the ECI's composition adjustment is good for understanding wage growth from a slack / business cycle perspective, \"the composition of recent job growth is tilted toward lower paying jobs\" is also a very important (but distinct) trend https://t.co/YGS4VguOnJ", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116161547651399989"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-30T13:09:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116155480842342416"], "id": "2116155480842342416", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 1760, "like_count": 17, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 6}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116153608869957710", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Every discussion of recently disappointing wage growth should stare at this chart for 10 seconds https://t.co/9LV1Pjvwr7", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116155480842342416"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-10-30T12:57:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116152564916060396"], "id": "2116152564916060396", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11508, "like_count": 17, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Our latest #OnInvesting podcast episode has dropped, on which @CollinMartinCS and I dissect the latest Fed meeting, as well as concerns about AI infiltrating both the equity and bond market: https://t.co/MFLCVUsTzk", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2116152564916060396"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-30T12:53:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116151581087572150"], "id": "2116151581087572150", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 3809, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Employment cost index recap:\n\n1/ First thing - the sharp recent wage deceleration we see in the monthly jobs report is absent from the employment cost index (ECI).\n\nThe wage deceleration is probably a composition artifact... https://t.co/xKYKrY6xJU", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116151581087572150"}], "inclu